      "message": "This seems wrong? GLSL\u0027s ternary conditionally evaluates the false/true expressions, whereas `select` evaluates both unconditionally. This is different from HLSL\u0027s ternary, which /does/ unconditionally evaluate both expressions.\n\nI think you can just emit this as `mix()`, which I believe has the same semantics as WGSL\u0027s select when you provide a boolean for the third argument.\n\nI see that the AST GLSL backend also uses a ternary for select, so I\u0027m guessing we don\u0027t have CTS coverage for this.",
